Discovered in the course of exploring the array API standard in #16099. All of this is on a Colab CPU backend, with JAX v0.4.20. Also reproduced locally on CPU at HEAD.
Simple repro of the main issue:
import jax
import jax.numpy as jnp

a = jnp.array([2396747., 2396747., 2396747.])
b = jnp.array([7., 7., 7.])

print(jnp.cross(a, b))
# [1. 1. 1.]

with jax.disable_jit():
  print(jnp.cross(a, b))
# [0. 0. 0.]
jnp.cross is JIT-compiled by default, and it looks like jit is causing an off-by-one error.
I was able to reduce this further to this simpler repro:
def f(a1, a2, b1, b2):
  return a1 * b2 - a2 * b1

a = 2396747.
b = 7.

print(f(a, a, b, b))
# 0.0

print(jax.jit(f)(a, a, b, b))
# 1.0
